WEBVTT

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.990
You're working in Sendai now, aren't you?

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:43.040
Yes.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.570
I saw some pictures.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.370
You stood out in them 
just like you always do.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.250
Of course, it's only natural since 
you were surrounded by amateurs.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.800
Hello, Sendai.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.460
We're the I-1 Club.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:01.470
Today, we have good news for you.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.650
The I-1 Club's

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:07.490
National 47 Prefecture Love 
Connection Project begins today.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.930
For this project, the I-1 Club 
will go to see you.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:12.020
I came here to check 
things out for our project.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:13.770
I see.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:19.780
Here in Miyagi Prefecture's Sendai, 
we'll be building a theater.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.100
We're so excited to see you.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.290
Look forward to it.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.290
This has been a message 
from the I-1 Club!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.040
Good luck.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.390
Even Shiraki-san 
is prioritizing this project.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.800
If we don't work hard, 
we'll be kicked out.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.210
Can I ask you something?

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.430
What?

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.570
I'm impressed you 
decided to come back.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.060
Why did you do it?

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:59.070
Well, you can do whatever you want.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.450
But don't forget 
the trouble you caused us.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.840
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.450
It's ready.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.840
It's piping hot and ready.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.600
As expected of Twinkle.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.820
Their work is fast, good, and cheap.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:32.120
I think it's only cheap 
because you haggled them down.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.980
Read these divine lyrics, girls.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:36.860
So hot.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.000
16-Year-Old Agape

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.900
I told you it's piping hot.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.860
Now that we have a second song, 
I thought we could make a splash.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.500
What?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:58.750
And so, we'll be performing a concert 
on May 25th at MACANA with our new song.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.960
Huh? I'm getting a sense of déjà vu...

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.150
Oh, right.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.840
At the end of last year, 
this person said the same thing

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.870
and ran off with all our money.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.770
I've been traumatized by live concerts.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.690
I'm breaking out in hives!

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.450
Shut up already.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.270
In any case, we're putting on a concert.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.360
I understand how Matsuda-san feels.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.320
I know.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.650
I hope you're not planning 
to deceive us again.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.280
Deceive us?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.960
You're still carrying on about that?

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.600
You're such small people.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.660
It's not a matter of size.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.660
Well, let's get cracking.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.520
NFW!

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.450
What does that mean?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.460
No freaking way.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.300
What?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.950
Our concert is scheduled 
for the same day as

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.520
the I-1 Club's Sendai Theater 
opening concert!

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:47.430
What?!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.430
<b>Kumagaiya</b>

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:48.600
This isn't good.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.430
Won't we lose customers to them?

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.440
We'll start practicing 
the new song tomorrow.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.940
Okay.

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:57.030
Later.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:57.470
Okay.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:58.460
See you later.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.750
Bye bye.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.370
What kind of snacks 
will we get to eat today?

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.450
You're such a glutton, Minami.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.200
<b>National 47 Prefecture 
Love Connection Project</b>

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.200
<b>Finally Arriving in Sendai</b>

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.200
<b>Opens at the I-1 Theater Sendai on 5/25!!</b>

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.740
Everywhere you look, it's I-1.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:16.330
<b>"We're Coming To See You."</b>

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.010
Their marketing campaign is crazy.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.380
They're just abusing their wealth.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.460
I-1 Club finally arrives in Sendai on 5/25!!

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.220
But it's amazing that they can do that.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.950
It's always money, money, money.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:34.730
<b>Senichiya</b>

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:34.730
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.730
There are things in this world 
you can't buy with money!

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.460
Spending money on advertising 
will help your sales,

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.830
but it won't last forever.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.040
After all, it costs money!

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.050
Is that right?

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.300
Nothing's most important 
than making an honest living.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:52.200
Even the I-1 Club was built 
by the passion of Shiraki,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:58.550
who had nothing going for him 
except his love of idols.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.180
The I-1 Club started as

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.020
a local "no money, no connections, 
no name" group from Oshiage.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:10.760
That was before Oshiage built its Skytree.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:14.770
Now it's something of a tourist spot.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.890
President, are you 
familiar with that era?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.810
Of course I am!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.820
I've been in this business 
for forty-five years!

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:22.390
Huh?

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:23.820
How old are you?

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.980
I've been doing this since a past life!

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:26.900
I see.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.070
They didn't have any theaters back then.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.000
They held guerrilla concerts in Azumabashi,

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.160
but there's no audience there.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.350
I'm saying there aren't 
any young people there.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.410
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.410
Yeah.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:42.030
But idols become popular 
through word of mouth.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.950
There were rumors of interesting 
girls in Azumabashi.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:50.410
Those rumors spread like wildfire, 
giving us the I-1 we have today.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.680
Their honest work moved people's 
hearts and gave birth to money.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.100
That's how it works.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.480
You're sounding 
strangely reasonable today.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.940
It's scaring me.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.560
I'll do it this time.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:05.940
What?

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.740
Nothing!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.700
I was talking to myself!

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.680
<b>Jera</b>

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.830
The I-1 Club is really amazing.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:21.460
Yeah.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.960
Their choreography 
is so well coordinated.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.710
Mayushi used to be part of that.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:30.340
You must be confused.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:35.430
Wake Up, Girls! doesn't exist 
without Shimada Mayu, does it?

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.140
I won't lose.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.990
To who? I-1?

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.010
Don't you think that 
will take some time?

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:43.350
I think we just have 
to do the best we can.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.650
You're right.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.670
Let's first think of how 
we can gather as large

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:48.010
an audience for 
our concert as possible.

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:48.880
Yeah.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:51.990
Maybe I'll reach out 
to my friends this time.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.720
That's not good enough.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.770
You can't approach 
this like you're trying

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:56.760
to fill some small theater.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:57.740
What do you mean?

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:01.120
We need to increase our number of fans.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.940
Yeah, but...

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.760
Yoppi, let's go.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.260
Okay, let's take a break!

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.540
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.350
Airi, you're always behind.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:17.890
Huh?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.010
Sorry. Where?

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.190
This part.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.550
Give it a try.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:30.850
There it is.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:31.690
That's not right.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.510
What? It's not?

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:34.700
Isn't it like this?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.570
Like this, Yoppi?

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:44.460
Huh?

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.220
What's wrong with Yoppi?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.070
Since our new song 
is coming together,

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:57.270
I thought we could decide what 
we're singing at the concert today.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.960
First, I think it goes 
without saying that we'll use

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.740
"Stand Up!" and "16-Year-Old Agape."

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:09.230
"Stand Up!"

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:09.230
"16-Year-Old Agape"

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:04.630
I'm sure you all know,

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.860
that's not nearly enough.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.230
So I want to choose 
a few more songs today.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.360
I know! I know!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.110
What about anime songs?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.530
I'm sure our fans will enjoy them.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.150
Anime songs? Don't you think 
that's too commonplace?

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:20.470
Other groups sing them quite a bit.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.860
I want to do something unexpected.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.030
What about "Hikarizuka"?

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.790
Would anyone enjoy that?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.050
I'd prefer folk songs like "Ishinomaki 
Chatsumi-uta" or "Ishinomaki Sendou-uta."

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.050
I don't know about that, either.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.160
I think the members of the 
folk song club would enjoy it.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:41.310
What should we do?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.060
"Stand Up!"

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.060
"16-Year-Old Agape"

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.260
Maybe anime songs.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:44.060
I know! I know!

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:48.420
In that case, I have something 
I've danced to at work.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.700
This concert isn't just for you.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.320
What? But it's really cute.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.080
Folk songs are cute, too.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.990
And <i>Hikarizuka'</i>s not 
so much cute as cool.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.080
Anime songs!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:09:59.850
Folk songs!

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:00.660
"Hikarizuka"!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.750
H-Hey!

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.730
Are you sure you don't need to step in?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:09.960
They're getting out of hand.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.170
It's fine.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.090
Now that they can say what they want,

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.210
they're taking another step forward.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.340
Let them fight.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.720
But we don't have 
many days to prepare.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:24.180
If we're doing hit songs, 
maybe we should do I-1 Club songs?

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:29.900
Sorry.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:31.500
It's fine.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.390
You don't need to apologize.

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.670
But with the I-1 Theater 
coming to Sendai,

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.240
I don't think there's any need 
for us to sing their songs.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:45.240
Don't you think we should 
show our own colors?

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:48.750
Yeah. Mayu's right.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:51.250
In that case, anime songs!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:52.490
Folk songs!

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:53.500
"Hikarizuka"!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.500
I told you...

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.520
"Stand Up!"

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:55.520
"16-Year-Old Agape"

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.920
Let's go, I-1! Run!

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.720
There are tears of joy,

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.760
but there's no such thing 
as smiling while running!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.190
But we always smile!

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:08.390
All the time, we smile!

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.790
Smile while eating!

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:10.520
Smile while sleeping!

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:11.990
Smile while dancing!

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.530
Smile while singing!

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:16.540
Attention!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.620
Number 456, you're out.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.630
Leave.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:44.260
15, 16, 17...

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:51.000
18, 19, 20...

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:57.010
I think things are coming together.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.690
Yoppi, how was my choreography?

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.540
It's gotten a lot better.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.320
Really? Great.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.680
I'm hungry.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:07.830
Can I have a snack?

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:10.790
I baked some cookies.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.820
Did you make these yourself?

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:15.560
Yes.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.210
Thanks for the food!

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:22.090
But I'll get fat if I have too many.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:27.130
I'm jealous of Minami 
in more than one way.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:32.590
Do you think they'll 
take all our customers?

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.700
I don't think we can beat them.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:37.160
What good will saying that now do?

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:40.290
By the way, have you seen the members 
they're bringing to the Sendai theater?

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:41.560
Yeah, I did!

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:45.110
All the most popular members 
of I-1 are coming, right?

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.320
Yeah.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.330
Shihocchi, Yoshimegu, 
Maimai, and Nanokasu.

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:54.040
They're all top-class girls.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.410
They're really giving it 
everything they have.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.330
Beating them seems 
all the more hopeless.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.710
Don't get too worked up.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:02.970
Let's get back to our lessons.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.380
There's no time to spare.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:06.750
You're right.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:07.390
Let's do it.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:08.590
Yeah.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:09.730
All right, let's do it.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.890
Let's go.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:17.840
<i>My hair freshly shampooed on Sunday</i>

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.860
<b>"Sorry we seem like amateurs!"</b>

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:23.570
<i>I met you on the way to the station</i>

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:31.080
<i>Believing in coincidences 
that seem like fate</i>

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:37.200
<i>I will call your name...</i>

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.200
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.880
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.130
1, 2, 3...

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.130
 Working hard?

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.600
Good morning.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.980
Could we watch you practice?

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:47.630
Okay.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.890
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.890
You want me to check on them?

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.350
If you're curious, 
you should go yourself.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.390
It's too much work.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:57.100
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.770
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.540
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.540
Sorry.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.290
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.320
1, 2, 3, 4.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:12.830
What did you think?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.080
If you could tell us what we 
did wrong, we'd appreciate it.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.450
It was kind of a mess.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.240
What?

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:21.330
First, you.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.790
Yes.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.640
You almost ran into 
someone and apologized.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:26.840
Yes.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.500
You need to make sure 
your audience doesn't notice that.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.110
In fact, you probably

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:34.720
almost ran into each other 
because you held your position.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:36.440
Yes.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.640
When that happens, gauge your distance.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.980
It's okay if you step out of line a little,

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.730
but make sure you get out of her way.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.480
Okay.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.960
The final step of leveling up is compassion.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:48.490
Okay.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.220
How do you imagine 
yourselves dancing right now?

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.680
First, we must 
synchronize our choreography...

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:55.530
Oh, and rhythm.

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:59.750
Yeah. I got that feeling, 
but that's not what I meant.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:00.750
Huh?

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:04.170
I was asking what it means 
to be Wake Up, Girls!

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:11.000
Are you guys fighting enough?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.430
You should tell each other 
what you want to say.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.950
You're part of the same group.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:19.900
Of course, sometimes 
you say too much to me.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.960
You should tell each other 
what you want to say.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.790
You're part of the same group.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.670
<i>It's not easy for me to say.</i>

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.920
<i>I need her to talk to me first.</i>

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:54.720
How did it look?

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.470
There's no one there.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:00.150
My nightmare became reality.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:02.670
And this is the wallpaper 
of the Sendai theater

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:04.980
my shikigami returned to me.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.180
What is this?

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.790
Is it packed?

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.190
That's right.

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:16.830
It's so unbelievably crowded, 
you can't even see the stage.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.650
I knew it would be like this,

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:21.000
but seeing the difference 
is depressing.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:23.420
We practiced hard.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.630
Let's have fun at our own concert.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.740
Yeah, you're right.

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:29.130
That's all we can do.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.640
We've been waiting for you!

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:46.150
Miyu-chan!

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.110
You can do it, WUG-chan!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:18.340
<i>Believing I could not dream</i>

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.350
Good evening, everyone!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.350
We're the I-1 Club!

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:26.910
Today is the first day 
of the glorious Sendai Theater

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.250
opening concert!

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:32.270
We'll be giving it 
everything we have,

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:34.770
so stick with us until the very end!

00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:41.370
Um... We're Wake Up, Girls!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.080
We're based in Sendai.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:49.080
The song you just heard was written 
by our seniors in the industry...

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.320
It was written by Twinkle.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:00.600
Shihocchi and I turned pale,

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:04.560
but for some reason, 
Maimai ate the ramen in silence.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.250
Don't tell them that!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:09.520
I guess I saw a demonstration 
of Maimai's nerves of steel.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:11.730
If you keep talking, I'll strangle you!

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:16.760
Lastly, please listen to our new song.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:22.600
Lastly, please listen to our new song.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:33.500
<i>Larger than love, 
a 16-Year-Old Agape</i>

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.640
Oh, well.

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.720
We practiced so much, too.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.100
We failed completely.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.030
We kept making mistakes.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:54.340
I'm sorry.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:57.230
You don't need to keep blaming yourself.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.780
I made plenty of mistakes in my emceeing, too.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:04.160
I'm sure the I-1 concert was a blast.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:18.590
Thank you.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:20.090
Sure.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.840
Thanks for your hard work!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:24.240
Thank you...

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.850
What's wrong? You seem down.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:28.730
You know how it went.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:33.000
What? Did you think 
you could take on I-1?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.610
You're not ready for that.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.070
Oh, come on. What?

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.960
After only one concert? 
You're pathetic.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:45.110
You'd ruin a celebration 
with those despondent faces.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.960
Let's disperse for today.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.800
The president told me to come, 
and she's not here.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.300
Is she the one who told us to come?

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.630
That's right.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:05.820
She suddenly said, "Let's go 
to the I-1 Sendai Theater!"

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:07.510
Just how mean is she?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.230
No, it's not like that.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:13.190
Tange-san's a little strange and 
irresponsible, but she's not mean.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:17.940
I think she wants you to take 
it one honest step at a time.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.200
That's what this was about.

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:23.240
What are you waiting for?

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:24.990
Let's go.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.990
We were waiting for you!

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:49.400
It's no wonder we lost.

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:52.090
I feel stupid for being depressed.

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:54.350
Thank you.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.810
Thank you.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.550
They're beyond our reach.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:00.020
But we'll beat them someday.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.820
We'll start over tomorrow.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.030
Huh? Where's the president?

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.750
She told us to go on ahead.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:10.010
Come back soon! 
We'll be waiting for you!

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:10.740
Do your best!

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.000
Mayu...

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:14.750
Mayu?

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.570
You came.

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.260
Yeah.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:26.190
I'll text you later.

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:27.140
Okay.

00:21:31.610 --> 00:21:33.270
Thank you.

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:39.580
This may not answer 
your question, but...

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:40.020
What?

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.480
I'm impressed you 
decided to come back.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:44.900
Why did you do it?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:50.870
I think I can finally like idols.

00:22:03.110 --> 00:22:04.550
What are you trying to say?

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:06.500
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:09.050
You should let me handle it.

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.930
To be continued

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.920
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:46.130 --> 00:23:48.760
No one's getting any better.

00:23:48.760 --> 00:23:50.360
Are you saying you are?

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.160
Of course I am.

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:52.650
I grow every day.

00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:53.300
Really?

00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:53.980
Even my body.

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:54.960
Even my breasts! Look!

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:57.380
I wonder if I should 
say something...

00:23:57.380 --> 00:24:00.250
The next episode is "Not Yet."

